-- US-3125: twenty-five sleep, baby, maternity, hosiery and rainwear brands.
--
-- Catalogues read 2026-09-07 with scripts/ops/shopify-brand-harvest.mjs. Same
-- rules as 00734 and 00739: a colour on five or more products, a brand with at
-- least eight such colours and no more than 35% plain colour words, base_color
-- and shade from the brand's own facet where it publishes one and
-- aspect-normalize's family table otherwise.
--
-- -- REGISTERED NUMBERS: EIGHT OF TWENTY-FIVE --------------------------------
--
--     Cozy Earth        RN 172568   Cozy Earth Holdings, Inc      [Apparel Bedding Towels]
--     Halfdays          RN 161978   Halfdays Apparel Corp         [Women's apparel]
--     Kyte Baby         RN 150833   KYTE BABY LLC                 [BABY LAYETTE & ACCESSORIES]
--     Little Sleepies   RN 153882   Little Sleepies LLC           [Baby Apparel]
--     Manduka           RN 136624   MANDUKA LLC                   [BLANKETS TOWELS PILLOWS T-SHIRTS]
--     Medelita          RN 132539   MEDELITA, LLC                 [LAB COATS AND MEDICAL SCRUBS]
--     PELAGIC           RN 109605   PELAGIC, LLC                  [TEE SHIRTS HATS JACKETS]
--     Rockmount         RN 16045    ROCKMOUNT RANCH WEAR MFG CO
--
-- -- A NEW REASON TO REFUSE: THE NUMBER IS OLDER THAN THE BRAND ---------------
--
-- Sheertex returns RN 14756 SHEERTEX HOSIERY MILL INC. The name is exact and
-- the industry is exact -- hosiery, for a brand that makes rip-resistant tights.
-- It is still refused, and the reason is the NUMBER.
--
-- RNs are issued in sequence and are not reused, so an RN cannot predate the
-- company holding it. Measured against this corpus: Rockmount registered at
-- 16045, Pendleton at 29685, Filson at 39126, Brooks Brothers at 99458, Stussy
-- at 94974, Kyte Baby at 150833 and Cozy Earth at 172568. The sequence tracks
-- when a company REGISTERED, not when it was founded -- Brooks Brothers dates
-- from 1818 and sits high, Rockmount from 1946 and sits low -- but the
-- direction that matters is one-way. A number down at 14756 was issued decades
-- before Sheertex existed (2017), so it belongs to an older namesake.
--
-- This is inferred from issue order across the numbers above, not read off a
-- published date. It is offered as a check to APPLY, not as a fact to cite: when
-- an RN looks far too low for a young brand, it is a different company.
--
-- -- THE OTHER SIXTEEN REFUSED -----------------------------------------------
--
-- Bandit Running, Colorful Standard, Freenote Cloth, Kindred Bravely, Moose
-- Knuckles, Organic Basics, Swiftwick, Tanner Goods and ThirdLove return
-- NOTHING. A legitimate absence.
--
-- goodr and Rains are the substring trap, eleven and twelve: "goodr" pulls
-- GoodRobe & Co and four GOODRICH companies; "Rains" pulls TWISTED ST-RAINS,
-- FREEDOM-RAINS, B-RAINS-TORM and RAIN-SHEDDER. Birdy Grey (Blue Jay Beach,
-- Inc) and Capezio (Cap Dancewear Ltd, plus a WPL-only CAPEZIO TAILORING CO
-- that is a tailor rather than the dancewear house) return an unrelated
-- registrant. Parachute returns five Parachute companies and none of them is
-- the bedding brand -- the Primitive shape from 00747, too many good candidates
-- rather than none.
--
-- BEIS is the Monos refusal from 00749 repeating exactly. The register holds
-- BEIS LLC with a broad apparel product line, and BEIS makes luggage. Same
-- rule: an exact name is not enough when the business is wrong. Two in two runs
-- makes this a pattern worth naming rather than a one-off.
--
-- Ingrid & Isabel is the closest call of the run. URSULA INGRID CARNEY is the
-- founder, and MATERNITY BODYWEAR is precisely what the label invented. But
-- "Isabel" is a distinctive token and it is absent, which is a replacement
-- rather than the addition that let Ulla Johnson through in 00749. A perfect
-- product line cannot supply a name that is not there.
--
-- -- COLOURS ----------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Seeded: banditrunning (57), birdygrey (139), cozyearth (87), halfdays (23), kytebaby (81), manduka (12), organicbasics (93), parachute (32), pelagic (29), rains (21), swiftwick (25), tannergoods (13), thirdlove (13).
-- Palette refused, too few or too plain: ingridandisabel (9, 56% plain), medelita (10, 40% plain), sheertex (4).
-- No colour survives the filter: beis (34 raw), capezio (0 raw), colorfulstandard (0 raw), freenotecloth (12 raw), goodr (0 raw), kindredbravely (6 raw), littlesleepies (0 raw), mooseknuckles (0 raw), rockmount (0 raw).
--
